      "entry": 0,
      "root": "Wedh 2",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "modern_form": "PIE *wedʰ- 'to push, strike' (Pokorny 1. u̯edh- 1115; Beekes *h₂wedʰh₁- 'push away, slay')",
      "note": "Pokorny's first u̯edh- 'to push, hit' (p. 1115, = WP I 254 f.) groups exactly Skt. vadhati/avadhīt 'strike, kill', Av. vada- 'wedge', vadar- 'weapon', vādāya- 'push back', Gk. ōthéō 'push'. AHD wedh- 'To push, strike ... Greek ōthein, to push: osmosis' gives the same set. Modern work (Beekes, via Wiktionary s.v. ὠθέω) reconstructs it with laryngeals as *h₂wedʰh₁-; this is the root Nourai means. It must not be confused with the homophonous *wedʰ- 'to lead, marry' (Pokorny 2. u̯edh-), which Wiktionary's *wedʰ- page treats; Nourai's '2' is his own numbering. Root, label and gloss are correct. The only soft points on the page are the gloss 'ax' for Av. vaδaγan- (attested only as a proper name) and the French link, since French osmose (1865) was taken from English osmosis rather than the other way round.",
      "note_fa": "ریشهٔ هندواروپایی آغازین *wedʰ- «هل دادن، زدن» (نزد پوکورنی 1. u̯edh-، ص ۱۱۱۵؛ بیکس با لارنگال‌ها *h₂wedʰh₁- «پس زدن، کشتن») است. سنسکریت vadhati «زدن، کشتن»، اوستایی vada- «گُوه»، vadar- «جنگ‌افزار» و vādāya- «پس راندن» و یونانی ōthéō «هل دادن» همه از آن‌اند. نباید آن را با *wedʰ- دیگر به معنای «بردن، زن گرفتن» یکی گرفت. ادعای نورایی دربارهٔ خود ریشه درست است.",
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ὠθέω",
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/wedʰ-"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {"ref": "POK:1115", "status": "supports", "note": "POK_full.txt line 88773 'Root / lemma: ued^-1 / Meaning: to push, hit / Material: Old Indie vadhati ... = Avestan vada- m. \"wedge zum Spalten des Holzes\", ... vadar- n. \"weapon (for hitting)\", ... Avestan vādaya- 'zurückstoßen' (lengthened grade as gr. ὠθέω) ... ὠθέω \"poke, push\"' ... 'Page(s):1115'."}
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {"src": "WLD", "where": "Bd. I p. 254 (WLD_Bd1_pages.txt leaf 263)", "stance": "supports", "note": "'1. uedh- „stoßen, schlagen“. Ai. vadhati ... av. vada- m. „Keil zum Spalten des Holzes“ ... av. vadar- n. „Waffe (zum Schlagen)“, av. vādaya- „zurückstoßen“ (dehnstufig wie gr. ὠθέω)'."},
        {"src": "AHD", "where": "AHD_watkins1985.txt line 1129", "stance": "supports", "note": "'wedh-. To push, strike. Suffixed lengthened o-grade form *wōdh-eyo- in Greek ōthein, to push: osmosis. [Pok. 1. uedh- 1115.]'"},
        {"src": "IEC", "where": "IEC.txt line 19814, uedh- (4)", "stance": "partial", "note": "Mann lists 'uedh- (4) \"fight\" ... Hes. cf. éthon ... \"striking\"; (alleged) étho, v. tr. \"strike\"' but does not cite ōthéō or the Avestan words; uedh- (1)/(2) are the 'marry/lead' roots."}
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "lang": "Avestan",
          "words": "vâdâya; vada; vadar; vadhğan",
          "verdict": "plausible",
          "derivation": "Gathic vādāya- 'to push back, keep off' (Y. 29.2 vādāyōit̰) is a causative-iterative with lengthened o-grade *wōdʰ-éye- (< *h₂wodʰh₁-éye-), the exact formal match of Greek ōthéō. Young Av. vada- m. 'wedge for splitting wood' (V. 14.7) = Skt. vadhá- 'deadly weapon', and vadar- n. 'weapon for striking' (Y. 32.10, 9.30) = Skt. vádhar- 'Indra's weapon'; both are regular *wedʰ-o-/*wedʰ-r̥ with Iranian dʰ > d. vaδaγan- (Nourai's vadhğan) is attested only as the name of a prince hostile to the faith (V. 19.6), identified with Aži Dahāka in Pahlavi texts. Bartholomae marks its meaning 'Eig. Bed.?' and Pokorny only asks whether it means 'axe, striker', so the gloss 'ax' is a guess. The first three words are confirmed, vadhğan 'ax' only plausible.",
          "derivation_fa": "اوستایی گاهانی vādāya- «پس راندن، دور داشتن» ستاک سببی با بالاندِ کشیدهٔ o (*wōdʰ-éye-) است و همتای دقیق یونانی ōthéō. اوستایی نو vada- «گُوهِ هیزم‌شکنی» و vadar- «جنگ‌افزار زدنی» با سنسکریت vadhá- و vádhar- هم‌ریشه‌اند و dʰ هندواروپایی در ایرانی d شده است. اما vaδaγan- تنها نام شاهی دین‌ستیز (یکی با ضحاک در متون پهلوی) است. بارتولومه معنایش را نامعلوم می‌داند و پوکورنی فقط می‌پرسد که آیا «تبر، زننده» است. پس سه واژهٔ نخست درست‌اند و معنای «تبر» برای vadhğan حدسی و با احتیاط پذیرفتنی است.",
          "sources": [
            "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ὠθέω"
          ],
          "ref_check": [
            {"ref": "POK:1115", "status": "supports", "note": "POK_full.txt line 88773ff.: 'Avestan vada- m. \"wedge zum Spalten des Holzes\", ... vadar- n. \"weapon (for hitting)\", ... Avestan vādaya- \"zurückstoßen\" ... is also Avestan vadayan- \"EN eines glaubensfeindlichen Fürsten\" as \"axe, Schläger\" to deuten?' Supports the first three words; for vadhğan Pokorny only asks the question."}
